The compilation environment doesn't have `ap_int.h` available as a standalone include — it comes transitively through `trmm.h` (which includes `<cmath>` but not ap types). Since the wide-bus approach requires HLS-specific types that aren't available in this compilation environment, the smallest correct fix is to revert to the original `double*` pointer interface (which does compile) while keeping all other optimizations (double-buffering, pipeline, unroll, array partitioning) intact.

